      "question": "Pull the latest oil sample for Transformer 1 at site MAIN and list which dissolved gases (hydrogen, methane, ethane, ethylene, acetylene, co) exceed the IEEE C57.104 Condition 1 single-gas limits. Also report the sample timestamp and how old the reading is. Only count combustible gases, and leave out co2, oxygen and nitrogen. If acetylene is missing from the newest record, use the most recent non-null acetylene value, give its timestamp separately, and say that it comes from an older sample.",
      "answer": "**Transformer 1 (site MAIN): latest oil sample**\n\n- **Sample timestamp:** 2024-01-19T00:00:00 (UTC)\n- **Age of reading:** about 85,183,531 s, which is about 986 days or 2.7 years. This is an old sample.\n- **Acetylene:** the newest record has an acetylene value, so no older sample was used.\n\n**Gases above the IEEE C57.104 Condition 1 single-gas limits** (2008 table limits)\n\n| Gas | Measured (ppm) | Condition 1 limit (ppm) | Exceeds? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Hydrogen (H\u2082) | 2,850 | 100 | **Yes** (~28\u00d7) |\n| Methane (CH\u2084) | 7,400 | 120 | **Yes** (~62\u00d7) |\n| Ethane (C\u2082H\u2086) | 5,470 | 65 | **Yes** (~84\u00d7) |\n| Ethylene (C\u2082H\u2084) | 16,650 | 50 | **Yes** (~333\u00d7) |\n| Acetylene (C\u2082H\u2082) | 7 | 1 | **Yes** (7\u00d7) |\n| Carbon monoxide (CO) | 32 | 350 | No |\n\n**Result:** 5 of the 6 combustible gases are above the limit: hydrogen, methane, ethane, ethylene and acetylene. CO is within its limit. CO\u2082, O\u2082 and N\u2082 were left out as you asked.\n\nThe limits above come from the IEEE C57.104 2008 table, not from any tool. In the older 1991 edition the acetylene limit is 35 ppm, so under that edition acetylene would not count as exceeded.",
      "score": {
        "scorer": "llm_judge",
        "passed": false,
        "score": 0.8,
        "rationale": "The agent skipped the expected confirmation steps (iot.sites and iot.asset_ids) before calling iot.latest_reading, and made a redundant acetylene-only latest_reading call even though acetylene was present and non-null in the newest record. Otherwise the data (timestamp 2024-01-19, age ~85.18M s / ~986 days), the exclusion of CO2/O2/N2, and the Condition 1 comparison (H2, CH4, C2H6, C2H4, C2H2 exceed; CO does not) are all correct and clearly presented. In future, verify site/asset existence first",
